{"audio": "1timothy-02.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 89467, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2267, "text": "1 Timothy, Chapter Two."}, {"start_ms": 2267, "end_ms": 17067, "text": "I exhort therefore, that, first of all, supplications, prayers, intercessions, and giving of thanks, be made for all men; For kings, and for all that are in authority; that we may lead a quiet and peaceable life in all godliness and honesty."}, {"start_ms": 17067, "end_ms": 25067, "text": "For this is good and acceptable in the sight of God our Saviour; Who will have all men to be saved, and to come unto the knowledge of the truth."}, {"start_ms": 25067, "end_ms": 34933, "text": "For there is one God, and one mediator between God and men, the man Christ Jesus; Who gave himself a ransom for all, to be testified in due time."}, {"start_ms": 34933, "end_ms": 43733, "text": "Whereunto I am ordained a preacher, and an apostle, (I speak the truth in Christ, and lie not;) a teacher of the Gentiles in faith and verity."}, {"start_ms": 43733, "end_ms": 50000, "text": "I will therefore that men pray every where, lifting up holy hands, without wrath and doubting."}, {"start_ms": 50000, "end_ms": 64800, "text": "In like manner also, that women adorn themselves in modest apparel, with shamefacedness and sobriety; not with broided hair, or gold, or pearls, or costly array; But (which becometh women professing godliness) with good works."}, {"start_ms": 64800, "end_ms": 67867, "text": "Let the woman learn in silence with all subjection."}, {"start_ms": 67867, "end_ms": 74267, "text": "But I suffer not a woman to teach, nor to usurp authority over the man, but to be in silence."}, {"start_ms": 74267, "end_ms": 77600, "text": "For Adam was first formed, then Eve."}, {"start_ms": 77600, "end_ms": 82267, "text": "And Adam was not deceived, but the woman being deceived was in the transgression."}, {"start_ms": 82267, "end_ms": 89467, "text": "Notwithstanding she shall be saved in childbearing